.TH QFW-SLURM-GATEWAY.YAML 5 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-gateway.yaml \- QSGP gateway service configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-gateway.yaml
selects the QSGP listener, authenticated caller policy, Slurm verifier, QFw
installation, and durable journal. The file must be owned by root and must not
be group- or world-writable.
.SH LISTEN
.TP
.B host
Listener hostname or address.
.TP
.B port
Listener TCP port.
.TP
.B max-credential-bytes
Maximum accepted MUNGE credential size.
.TP
.B max-frame-bytes
Maximum decoded QSGP frame size.
.TP
.B connect-timeout-seconds
Bound for external connection setup.
.TP
.B request-timeout-seconds
Absolute gateway operation bound.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.TP
.B mechanism
Must be
.BR munge .
.TP
.B accepted-uids
User names or numeric UIDs permitted to originate lifecycle requests. A normal
site includes root for remote SPANK callbacks and the configured Slurm
controller user for epilog requests.
.TP
.B expected-plugin-name
Authenticated QSGP caller name. The current protocol uses
.BR spank_quantum .
.SH SLURM
.TP
.B cluster-name
Exact cluster name accepted in requests and queried through slurmctld.
.TP
.B command
Path or command name for the JSON-capable
.B scontrol
client.
.SH QFW
.TP
.B activation
Absolute path to the selected
.B qfw-activate
script.
.TP
.B venv
Absolute path to the Python environment containing QFw, DEFw, and the gateway.
.TP
.B site-config
Absolute path to the QFw site YAML file. Its directory connection record is
used by
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway-launch (8).
.SH JOURNAL
.TP
.B path
Absolute path to the protected SQLite reservation journal. The gateway service
account must own its parent directory.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
listen:
  host: 0.0.0.0
  port: 18095
  max-credential-bytes: 65536
  max-frame-bytes: 262144
  connect-timeout-seconds: 5
  request-timeout-seconds: 120

authentication:
  mechanism: munge
  accepted-uids: [root, slurm]
  expected-plugin-name: spank_quantum

slurm:
  cluster-name: qfw-cluster
  command: scontrol

qfw:
  activation: /opt/openqse/qfw/bin/qfw-activate
  venv: /opt/openqse/qfw-venv
  site-config: /etc/openqse/qfw/site.yaml

journal:
  path: /var/lib/qfw-slurm-gateway/reservations.sqlite3
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qfw-slurm/gateway.yaml
Conventional installed configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qfw-slurm/config/gateway.yaml.example
Packaged example when the installation prefix is
.IR /usr .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-plugin.conf (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway (8),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway-launch (8)
